{"parentUuid":"93124304-31d0-405b-8faa-d78f1bece310","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Shrn8RQXHoxt3MpaivTFxR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**.mjs = ES6 modules nativement.**\n\nPar défaut, Node.js traite les `.js` comme CommonJS (`require()`, `module.exports`). Un `.mjs` force ES6 modules (`import`, `export`) sans avoir besoin de `package.json` avec `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n\n**Comparaison :**\n\n```js\n// CommonJS (.js)\nconst fs = require('fs')\nmodule.exports = { foo: 1 }\n\n// ES6 (.mjs)\nimport fs from 'fs'\nexport const foo = 1\n```\n\n**Avantages `.mjs` pour auto-update :**\n\n| Aspect | CommonJS | ES6 (.mjs) |\n|--------|----------|-----------|\n| Syntax | `require` (verbeux) | `import` (moderne) |\n| Async-first | Compliqué | `top-level await` ✓ |\n| Config | Besoin de `package.json` | Standalone |\n| Top-level await | ✗ | ✓ |\n\n**Exemple pertinent — top-level await :**\n\n```mjs\n// Standalone, aucun package.json nécessaire\nimport { execSync } from 'child_process'\nimport fs from 'fs'\n\n// Peut attendre directement, sans async wrapper\nconst status = await execSync('git status --porcelain')\nconsole.log(status.toString())\n```\n\nVs CommonJS = obligé de wrapper dans `async () => {}`.\n\n**Pour toi :** `.mjs` = moins de boilerplate, vraiment utile pour des petits scripts d'auto-update lancés via LaunchAgent (0 dépendances, 0 config, directement exécutable).\n\n**Décision ?** Toujours Option A (watcher local) ?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1187,"cache_read_input_tokens":95650,"output_tokens":593,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1187,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":593,"cache_read_input_tokens