{"parentUuid":"2c7e00e2-9956-4ea8-9905-4d1239fd448a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01A374i7A42pssstCsmzKWzi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P3fENcSLY5wkEYpJUbK7qq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/auto-git-push && cat > /tmp/auto-git-push/README.md << 'EOF'\n# auto-git-push\n\nAuto-commit and push any local git repo on file change — zero dependencies, pure Node.js built-ins.\n\nDesigned for config repos, notes, memory files, or any folder you want automatically backed up to GitHub.\n\n---\n\n## How it works\n\nA small Node.js script (`autoupdate.mjs`) watches one or more local folders using the built-in `fs.watch` API.\n\nWhen any file changes:\n1. Waits 3 seconds (debounce — avoids commit-per-keystroke)\n2. Runs `git add -A`\n3. Checks if anything is actually staged\n4. If yes: `git commit -m \"auto-sync <hostname> <timestamp>\"` then `git push`\n\nA macOS LaunchAgent (`com.zenray.autoupdate.plist`) keeps the script running at all times — starts at login, restarts on crash.\n\n**Respects `.gitignore`** — `git add -A` never stages what you've excluded.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements\n\n- macOS\n- Node.js (`brew install node`)\n- `git` configured with push access (SSH key or HTTPS token)\n\n---\n\n## Install\n\n### 1. Copy `autoupdate.mjs`\n\nPlace it anywhere permanent. Recommended: `~/.claude/autoupdate.mjs`\n\n```bash\ncurl -o ~/.claude/autoupdate.mjs \\\n  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/matthieuhuguet/auto-git-push/main/autoupdate.mjs\n```\n\n### 2. Edit the repos list\n\nOpen `autoupdate.mjs` and update the `REPOS` array:\n\n```js\nconst REPOS = [\n  resolve(os.homedir(), '.claude'),\n  resolve(os.homedir(), 'Create/Build/Memory'),\n  // add any repo path here\n]\n```\n\n### 3. Install the LaunchAgent\n\n```bash\n# Copy the plist\ncp com.zenray.autoupdate.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/\n\n# Edit the node path and script path if needed\n# Default: /opt/homebrew/bin/node (Homebrew on Apple Silicon)\n# Check yours: which node\n\n# Load it\nlaunchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.zenray.autoupdate.plist\n```\n\n### 4. Verify it's running\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl list | grep autoupdate\n# Should show: <PID>  0  com.zenray.autoupdate\n\ntail -f ~/.claude/autoupdate.log\n```\n\n---\n\n## Logs\n\n| File | Content |\n|------|---------|\n| `~/.claude/autoupdate.log` | All events (started, pushed, skipped, errors) |\n| `~/.claude/autoupdate.error.log` | Stderr from Node.js |\n\n---\n\n## Stop / restart\n\n```bash\n# Stop\nlaunchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.zenray.autoupdate.plist\n\n# Start\nlaunchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.zenray.autoupdate.plist\n\n# Restart\nlaunchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.zenray.autoupdate.plist && \\\nlaunchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.zenray.autoupdate.plist\n```\n\n---\n\n## Add a new repo\n\nEdit `REPOS` in `autoupdate.mjs`, then restart the LaunchAgent.\n\n---\n\n## Notes\n\n- Debounce is 3 seconds. Change `DEBOUNCE_MS` at the top of the script.\n- Submodules with untracked content are silently skipped (won't block the push).\n- Commit message format: `auto-sync <hostname> YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`\n- Designed for small text repos (config, notes, markdown). Not for large binaries.\nEOF\necho \"done\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":183,"cache_read_input_tokens":78036,"output_tokens":1032,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":183,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1032,"cache_read_input_tokens":78036,"cache_creation_input_tokens":183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":183},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_